  "about": "The order state machine (orders/state.ts) as used by cancelOrder, adminUpdateOrder, adminSetImeis and expireUnpaidOrders. Ported from supabase/tests/orders.test.sql (cancel_order, admin_update_order, admin_set_imeis), supabase/tests/refund_by_staff.test.sql (Mark refunded), supabase/tests/payments.test.sql (expiry, paid cancel) and scripts/api_e2e.py lifecycle and input checks, with the SQL in supabase/migrations/20261028000200_rpcs.sql and 20261030000350_refund_by_staff.sql. Transitions: pending_payment->cancelled; confirmed->packed|cancelled; packed->shipped|cancelled; shipped->delivered; delivered->refunded; cancelled+paid->refunded (paymentStatus only); same status = courier/tracking edit. Every world order belongs to alice. \"expect\": {} means the call succeeds and nothing in its reply is asserted. Arrays in \"expect\"/\"then\" match element by element, in order, and must have the same length (so a listed events[] also says how many events there are); each element is itself a deep-partial match. In \"then\", null means the field is absent or null. \"given\" docs are whole documents (they replace the world doc).",
